  "summary": "FrostyNeighbor (aka Ghostwriter, UNC1151, TA445) ran a March 2026 campaign against Ukrainian governmental organizations using spearphishing PDFs that, after server-side victim validation, deliver a RAR with a first-stage JavaScript dropper and a JavaScript PicassoLoader downloader. PicassoLoader fingerprints the host over HTTPS, receives a scheduled-task XML template and a third stage that writes a base64 Cobalt Strike beacon to %ProgramData%\\ViberPC.dll, masquerading a copy of rundll32.exe as ViberPC.exe and persisting via a Run key and scheduled task. Detection can focus on the bespoke C2 URIs, the WinDataScope/ViberPC file and registry names, and the SettingTimeAPI DLL export.",
